     1,
     "<font size=\"2\" face=\"sans-serif\">Hi Keith,</font>\r\n<br>\r\n<br><font size=\"2\" face=\"sans-serif\">Does this do it? </font>\r\n<br>\r\n<br><font size=\"2\" face=\"sans-serif\">ggplot(tst,aes(X10..400,1 - ecdf(X10..400)(X10..400)))+geom_step()</font>\r\n<br>\r\n<br><font size=\"2\" face=\"sans-serif\">The only drawback is, you can&#39;t make\r\nuse of the grouping - which is what&#39;s so nice about stat_ecdf. So you&#39;d\r\nhave to make a separate plot for each variable unless someone else here\r\nknows an alternative. </font>\r\n<br>\r\n<br><font size=\"2\" face=\"sans-serif\">Here&#39;s the data again in case anyone\r\nneeds it:</font>\r\n<br>\r\n<br><font size=\"2\" face=\"sans-serif\">tst&lt;-structure(list(X10..400 = c(-18.1392534702245,\r\n14.1246921733071, </font>\r\n<br>"
