     "<font size=\"1\" color=\"#000080\" face=\"sans-serif\"><b>Adam Loveland</b></font><font size=\"1\" color=\"#000080\" face=\"sans-serif\"><b><br>\r\n</b></font>\r\n<br>\r\n<br>\r\n<br>\r\n<table width=\"100%\">\r\n<tr valign=\"top\">\r\n<td><font size=\"1\" color=\"#5f5f5f\" face=\"sans-serif\">From:</font>\r\n<td><font size=\"1\" face=\"sans-serif\">Keith Weintraub &lt;<a href data-email-masked rel=\"nofollow\">kw1...@gmail.com</a>&gt;</font>\r\n<tr valign=\"top\">\r\n<td><font size=\"1\" color=\"#5f5f5f\" face=\"sans-serif\">To:</font>\r\n<td><font size=\"1\" face=\"sans-serif\"><a href data-email-masked rel=\"nofollow\">adam.l...@pnc.com</a></font>\r\n<tr valign=\"top\">\r\n<td><font size=\"1\" color=\"#5f5f5f\" face=\"sans-serif\">Date:</font>\r\n<td><font size=\"1\" face=\"sans-serif\">02/14/2013 09:21 AM</font>\r\n<tr valign=\"top\">\r\n<td><font size=\"1\" color=\"#5f5f5f\" face=\"sans-serif\">Subject:</font>\r\n<td><font size=\"1\" face=\"sans-serif\">Re: Plotting ecdf</font></td></td></tr></td></td></tr></td></td></tr></td></td></tr></table>\r\n<br>\r\n<hr noshade>\r\n<br>\r\n<br>\r\n<br><font size=\"3\">Adam,</font>\r\n<br><font size=\"3\">  Thanks for the help.</font>\r\n<br>\r\n<br><font size=\"3\">Yes it&#39;s nice to have the &quot;ecdf&quot;</font>\r\n<br>\r\n<br><font size=\"3\">I would like to also see what is called an &quot;Exceedance\r\nCurve&quot; that is used in actuarial settings. I think it is just 1 -\r\necdf. It shows the probability of loss of X will be exceeded.</font>\r\n<br>\r\n<br><font size=\"3\">Take care,</font>\r\n<br><font size=\"3\">Thanks again,</font>\r\n<br><font size=\"3\">KW </font>\r\n<br><font size=\"2\" face=\"Comic Sans MS\"><br>\r\n--</font><font size=\"3\"> </font>\r\n<br>"
