     "\r\n<br><font size=\"3\">On Feb 13, 2013, at 10:20 AM, </font><a href data-email-masked rel=\"nofollow\"><font size=\"3\" color=\"blue\"><u>adam.l...@pnc.com</u></font></a><font size=\"3\">\r\nwrote:</font>\r\n<br>\r\n<br><font size=\"2\" face=\"sans-serif\">Hi,</font><font size=\"3\"> <br>\r\n</font><font size=\"2\" face=\"sans-serif\"><br>\r\nHere:</font><font size=\"3\"> <br>\r\n</font><font size=\"2\" face=\"sans-serif\"><br>\r\ntst.melt&lt;-melt(tst)</font><font size=\"3\"> </font><font size=\"2\" face=\"sans-serif\"><br>\r\nggplot(tst.melt,aes(value))+stat_ecdf(aes(group=variable))+facet_wrap(~variable)</font><font size=\"3\">\r\n<br>\r\n</font><font size=\"2\" face=\"sans-serif\"><br>\r\nThey recently added stat_ecdf to ggplot2. I was happy they did. </font><font size=\"3\"><br>\r\n<br>\r\n<br>\r\n<br>\r\n</font><font size=\"1\" color=\"#000080\" face=\"sans-serif\"><b><br>\r\nAdam Loveland</b></font><font size=\"3\"><br>\r\n<br>\r\n<br>\r\n<br>\r\n</font>\r\n<table width=\"100%\">\r\n<tr valign=\"top\">\r\n<td width=\"13%\"><font size=\"1\" color=\"#5f5f5f\" face=\"sans-serif\">From:</font><font size=\"3\">\r\n</font>\r\n<td width=\"86%\"><font size=\"1\" face=\"sans-serif\">Keith Weintraub &lt;</font><a href data-email-masked rel=\"nofollow\"><font size=\"1\" color=\"blue\" face=\"sans-serif\"><u>kw1...@gmail.com</u></font></a><font size=\"1\" face=\"sans-serif\">&gt;</font><font size=\"3\">\r\n</font>\r\n<tr valign=\"top\">\r\n<td><font size=\"1\" color=\"#5f5f5f\" face=\"sans-serif\">To:</font><font size=\"3\">\r\n</font>\r\n<td><font size=\"1\" face=\"sans-serif\">&quot;</font><a href data-email-masked rel=\"nofollow\"><font size=\"1\" color=\"blue\" face=\"sans-serif\"><u>ggp...@googlegroups.com</u></font></a><font size=\"1\" face=\"sans-serif\">&quot;\r\n&lt;</font><a href data-email-masked rel=\"nofollow\"><font size=\"1\" color=\"blue\" face=\"sans-serif\"><u>ggp...@googlegroups.com</u></font></a><font size=\"1\" face=\"sans-serif\">&gt;</font><font size=\"3\">\r\n</font>\r\n<tr valign=\"top\">\r\n<td><font size=\"1\" color=\"#5f5f5f\" face=\"sans-serif\">Date:</font><font size=\"3\">\r\n</font>\r\n<td><font size=\"1\" face=\"sans-serif\">02/12/2013 11:31 PM</font><font size=\"3\">\r\n</font>\r\n<tr valign=\"top\">\r\n<td><font size=\"1\" color=\"#5f5f5f\" face=\"sans-serif\">Subject:</font><font size=\"3\">\r\n</font>\r\n<td><font size=\"1\" face=\"sans-serif\">Plotting ecdf</font><font size=\"3\"> </font>\r\n<tr valign=\"top\">\r\n<td><font size=\"1\" color=\"#5f5f5f\" face=\"sans-serif\">Sent by:</font><font size=\"3\">\r\n</font>\r\n<td><a href data-email-masked rel=\"nofollow\"><font size=\"1\" color=\"blue\" face=\"sans-serif\"><u>ggp...@googlegroups.com</u></font></a></td></td></tr></td></td></tr></td></td></tr></td></td></tr></td></td></tr></table>\r\n<br><font size=\"3\"><br>\r\n</font>\r\n<hr noshade><font size=\"3\"><br>\r\n<br>\r\n<br>\r\nFolks, <br>\r\n  What would be the best way to plot the ecdf of each of these columns\r\nin a single chart? <br>\r\n<br>\r\nHow about if I want to put each ecdf in its own panel in some kind of 3x3\r\ndisplay with all the x and y limits the same? <br>\r\n<br>\r\nWhat if I want to reverse the direction of the ecdf, sometimes this is\r\ncalled an exceedance chart. <br>\r\n<br>\r\nThanks for your time, <br>\r\nKW <br>\r\n<br>\r\nstructure(list(X10..400 = c(-18.1392534702245, 14.1246921733071, <br>\r\n20.105156515452, -10.0293056051522, 79.9780787509287, -5.79954954730988,\r\n<br>\r\n-11.9427084290315, -8.58958279843375, -21.2841326927118, -15.5914374283893,\r\n<br>\r\n20.2076342432622, -48.2013769264652, 15.5326574147055, -10.8033879714582,\r\n<br>\r\n-1.51607248432964, -8.03592971988138, 18.7819921838991, 5.20486855055492,\r\n<br>\r\n20.3417197605472, 6.48074165849215), X25..400 = c(0, 21.7745681446661,\r\n<br>\r\n37.1672350655981, -37.061948148269, 209.966637661476, -27.1403695719935,\r\n<br>\r\n-41.4974948557998, -33.7028629342175, -62.6844768016134, -49.8652